			<div class="content" id="post-content-3760472">
									

<p>This feels like a collage of typical horror elements, most of them ill-defined, resulting in a piece that feels like it's treading common ground while being thematically lost. There's a whole lot of loose ends and ill-defined characters, with the strong point probably being the first interview. The neck-scratching initially seemed interesting enough, particularly since one of the Foundation guys was affected by the end&#8230; and that's it. The implications of this aren't addressed at all. Does the agent share the same fate as Sheldon at the end? If so, what does that mean? Why should I care?</p>
<p>I can't fault the pacing and it did generally hold my interest until the end. There's also a lot of good imagery here, and the central premise is&#8230; ok, I guess? At least from what I gathered. At any rate, I understand some of the choices you made here, but ultimately I've seen this sort of thing on the site enough times that this doesn't work for me in its current state.</p>

