<blockquote>
<p><em>(Delgado scratches behind his ear, looking at the ground.)</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is correct.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>(Delgado begins itching a point his neck)</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>On</strong> his neck would fix the sentence as a whole, but this is still incorrect; unless Delgado is telling you that he has an itch, he's <em>scratching</em> his neck.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Parsons now randomly will <strong>itch</strong> his neck a number of times throughout the episode.<br />
Now, rarely, single-frame black screens bearing the word RABBIT in dark blue text will appear, at which point Parsons will repeatedly <strong>scratch</strong> at a point on his throat until he is able to tear a small hole in the skin.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I have several other issues with this, mostly echoing what's already been noted above, but felt obliged to include this nugget as it seems no one else had yet.</p>

